Review by Samira Aubakirova

I followed this guide to set up a test virtual machine using VirtualBox and Ubuntu. The instructions were clear and easy to follow, especially because of the screenshots.

I started by installing VirtualBox and downloading Ubuntu. Then I created a VM with 2 CPUs, 2 GB of RAM, and 20 GB of storage.

During the installation, I faced two small problems. First, Ubuntu took longer to install than I expected, and I thought it was frozen. I waited a little longer, and it continued normally. Second, the internet connection wasn’t working at first. I checked the network settings, switched to NAT, and restarted the VM, which fixed the issue.

After that, everything worked fine. I also created a snapshot called “Clean Install” so I could restore the system if something went wrong.

Overall, I think this is a useful guide for beginners. The steps are simple and well-explained, but adding some troubleshooting tips would make it even better.
